---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteExtras from '@/components/SiteExtras.astro';
import '@/styles/research-primer.css';
import '@/styles/research-field-guide.css';
import { withBase } from '@/utils/url';
---
<BaseLayout title="Inventory Theory" active="Research">
  <main class="site-shell research-primer-page field-guide-page">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="ui-copy-en">Field guide · 01</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">领域导览 · 01</span></div>
      <h1>Inventory Theory</h1>
      <p class="field-guide-lede">
        <span class="ui-copy-en">Inventory theory studies how much stock to hold, when to replenish it, and where to place it when supply and demand do not line up perfectly in time. The field is much larger than “keeping a warehouse full”: it is a theory of buffers, timing, information, service, and risk.</span>
        <span class="ui-copy-zh">库存理论研究的是，当供给与需求无法在时间上完美对齐时，我们应该持有多少库存、什么时候补货、把库存放在哪里。它远不只是“仓库里放多少货”，更是一套关于缓冲、时间、信息、服务水平与风险的决策理论。</span>
      </p>
      <div class="field-guide-meta">
        <span><span class="ui-copy-en">Inventory control</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">库存控制</span></span>
        <span><span class="ui-copy-en">Supply chains</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">供应链</span></span>
        <span><span class="ui-copy-en">Service systems</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">服务系统</span></span>
        <span><span class="ui-copy-en">Stochastic models</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">随机模型</span></span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="field-guide-orientation">
      <span>30,000 FT</span>
      <p>
        <span class="ui-copy-en">The central tension is simple: stock protects a system from mismatch and uncertainty, but stock is costly. Inventory theory asks when that protection is worth paying for, how the answer changes with information and lead time, and what policy can implement the answer repeatedly.</span>
        <span class="ui-copy-zh">这个领域最核心的矛盾其实很简单：库存可以保护系统免受供需错配与不确定性的冲击，但库存本身也有成本。库存理论要回答的是，这份保护什么时候值得买、信息与提前期会怎样改变答案，以及怎样把答案变成可以反复执行的补货策略。</span>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="field-guide-section">
      <div class="field-guide-section-head">
        <span class="field-guide-index">01</span>
        <div>
          <h2><span class="ui-copy-en">What problem is inventory solving?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">库存到底在解决什么问题？</span></h2>
          <p><span class="ui-copy-en">Inventory exists because production, transportation, purchasing, and demand occur at different times and with different degrees of uncertainty.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">库存之所以存在，是因为生产、运输、采购与需求发生在不同时间，而且它们的不确定性也不同。</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="field-guide-prose">
        <p><span class="ui-copy-en">A retailer cannot instantly manufacture every item the moment a customer asks for it. A factory may produce in batches. A hospital keeps critical supplies before an emergency arrives. A spare-parts network stocks components even though most of them will not be used today. In each case, inventory separates two processes that would otherwise need to be perfectly synchronized.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">零售商不可能在顾客提出需求的那一刻才即时制造商品；工厂往往需要批量生产；医院必须在急诊发生以前就准备关键耗材；备件网络会存放大量今天未必会用到的零件。它们背后的共同点是，库存把两个原本必须完美同步的过程分开了。</span></p>
        <p><span class="ui-copy-en">That separation creates a trade-off. More inventory usually means better availability and less disruption, but it also ties up capital, occupies space, risks obsolescence, and may create waste. The interesting question is therefore not whether inventory is “good” or “bad”, but how much buffering a particular system should buy.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">但这种分离会带来新的权衡。更多库存通常意味着更高的可得性和更少的中断，同时也意味着资金占用、仓储、过时和浪费。因此真正的问题不是库存到底“好不好”，而是一个具体系统究竟应该为多少缓冲能力付费。</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="field-guide-question-grid">
        <article class="field-guide-question"><span>Q1</span><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">How much?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">备多少？</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Choose order quantities or target stock levels that balance shortage risk against holding and ordering costs.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">决定订货量或目标库存水平，在缺货风险、持有成本和订货成本之间权衡。</span></p></article>
        <article class="field-guide-question"><span>Q2</span><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">When?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">什么时候补？</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Decide whether replenishment happens continuously, periodically, after a threshold is crossed, or on a fixed review schedule.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">决定补货是连续触发、周期检查、越过阈值后触发，还是按固定计划进行。</span></p></article>
        <article class="field-guide-question"><span>Q3</span><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">Where?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">放在哪里？</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Allocate stock across warehouses, retailers, service locations, and echelons so that the network can respond where demand appears.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">在仓库、零售点、售后节点以及多级供应链之间分配库存，使系统能够在需求真正出现的位置响应。</span></p></article>
        <article class="field-guide-question"><span>Q4</span><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">With what information?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">依据什么信息？</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Use demand history, lead times, forecasts, product age, pipeline stock, capacity, and service commitments without making the state unnecessarily complicated.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">利用需求历史、提前期、预测、产品年龄、在途库存、产能与服务承诺，同时又避免让决策状态复杂到不可计算。</span></p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="field-guide-section">
      <div class="field-guide-section-head">
        <span class="field-guide-index">02</span>
        <div>
          <h2><span class="ui-copy-en">The main model families</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">库存理论的主要模型家族</span></h2>
          <p><span class="ui-copy-en">Different models are not a list of unrelated formulas. Each one isolates a different source of timing, uncertainty, or operational friction.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">不同库存模型不是一堆互不相关的公式。每一类模型都在突出一种不同的时间机制、不确定性或运营摩擦。</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="field-guide-atlas">
        <article class="field-guide-card"><small>01 · deterministic</small><h3>EOQ & lot sizing</h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">When demand is relatively predictable, the classic question is how to balance fixed ordering or setup costs against inventory carried between replenishments.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">当需求相对可预测时，经典问题是如何在固定订货或启动成本与批量补货造成的库存持有之间权衡。</span></p></article>
        <article class="field-guide-card"><small>02 · one period</small><h3>Newsvendor</h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">A single decision is made before uncertain demand is known. The critical trade-off is overage versus underage, making it a basic model of capacity and inventory under uncertainty.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">在随机需求揭晓前只做一次决策。核心是多备一单位和少备一单位分别会造成什么损失，因此它也是很多产能与收益管理问题的原型。</span></p></article>
        <article class="field-guide-card"><small>03 · repeated review</small><h3>Base-stock / order-up-to</h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">In recurring systems, decisions are made period after period. Under important conditions, the optimal policy has a simple form: replenish inventory position toward a target level.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">在重复运营的系统中，决策每一期都会发生。在许多重要条件下，最优策略具有非常简单的结构：把库存位置补到某个目标水平。</span></p></article>
        <article class="field-guide-card"><small>04 · fixed costs</small><h3>(s,S), (Q,r)</h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">When placing an order itself has a fixed cost, it can be optimal to wait and then replenish in a batch. Threshold and reorder-point policies capture that logic.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">当“下单这件事”本身有固定成本时，系统往往不会每次少一点就补，而是先等到阈值，再一次补一批。阈值与再订货点策略描述了这种逻辑。</span></p></article>
        <article class="field-guide-card"><small>05 · networks</small><h3>Multi-echelon inventory</h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Stock is distributed across plants, central warehouses, regional depots, and retailers. A unit held upstream can protect several downstream locations, creating coordination questions.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">库存分布在工厂、中央仓、区域仓和零售点等多个层级。上游的一单位库存可能同时保护多个下游节点，因此会产生网络协同问题。</span></p></article>
        <article class="field-guide-card"><small>06 · special systems</small><h3>Perishable, spare-parts & service</h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Expiration, repair, substitution, low-frequency failures, installed bases, and service-level commitments create inventory problems whose state and cost structures differ sharply from ordinary retail stock.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">保质期、维修、替代、低频失效、在役产品群体以及服务水平承诺，会形成与普通零售库存很不一样的状态与成本结构。</span></p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="field-guide-section">
      <div class="field-guide-section-head">
        <span class="field-guide-index">03</span>
        <div>
          <h2><span class="ui-copy-en">What assumptions change the answer?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">哪些假设会真正改变库存策略？</span></h2>
          <p><span class="ui-copy-en">Inventory research often advances by changing one modelling ingredient and asking whether the policy structure, value of information, or computational difficulty changes with it.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">库存研究经常通过改变某个关键建模要素，观察策略结构、信息价值或计算难度是否随之变化。</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="field-guide-spectrum">
        <div class="field-guide-spectrum-row"><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">Demand</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">需求</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Deterministic, stochastic, seasonal, correlated, censored, learned from data, or affected by price and stock availability.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">可以是确定需求、随机需求、季节需求、相关需求、被缺货截断的需求，也可能需要从数据中学习，甚至受价格与库存可得性影响。</span></p><small>uncertainty</small></div>
        <div class="field-guide-spectrum-row"><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">Lead time</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">提前期</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Zero, fixed, random, capacity-dependent, or disrupted. Lead time determines how long a decision must protect the system before new supply can arrive.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">可以为零、固定、随机、受产能影响，或者被中断。提前期决定一次库存决策必须保护系统多长时间。</span></p><small>timing</small></div>
        <div class="field-guide-spectrum-row"><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">Shortage handling</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">缺货如何处理</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Demand may wait as backorders, disappear as lost sales, trigger emergency procurement, or damage a service-level target.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">缺货需求可以等待形成欠货，也可能直接流失，还可能触发紧急采购，或者影响服务水平约束。</span></p><small>service</small></div>
        <div class="field-guide-spectrum-row"><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">Product structure</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">产品结构</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Items may perish, become obsolete, substitute for one another, share components, or return through reverse logistics.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">产品可能腐坏、过时、彼此替代、共享零部件，也可能通过退货或逆向物流重新回到系统。</span></p><small>physics</small></div>
        <div class="field-guide-spectrum-row"><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">Network & capacity</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">网络与产能</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Warehouses interact through shared suppliers, transportation constraints, production capacity, lateral transshipment, and allocation rules.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">多个节点会通过共享供应商、运输限制、生产能力、横向调拨与分配规则相互影响。</span></p><small>system</small></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="field-guide-section">
      <div class="field-guide-section-head">
        <span class="field-guide-index">04</span>
        <div>
          <h2><span class="ui-copy-en">Why inventory theory cares about policy structure</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">为什么库存理论特别重视“策略结构”？</span></h2>
          <p><span class="ui-copy-en">The goal is rarely to compute one isolated order quantity. A useful theory explains how the decision should react whenever the system state changes.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">研究目标通常不是算出某一次应该订多少，而是解释当系统状态变化时，决策应该怎样随之变化。</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="field-guide-prose">
        <p><span class="ui-copy-en">This is why results such as base-stock levels, reorder points, monotonicity, convexity, and threshold policies matter. A structural result compresses a potentially huge optimization problem into an interpretable rule. It can tell a manager not only what to do for one numerical instance, but how the action should move when inventory, cost, lead time, or risk changes.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">这也是为什么基库存、再订货点、单调性、凸性与阈值策略在库存理论里如此重要。一个结构性结论可以把原本庞大的优化问题压缩成可解释的规则。它不仅告诉管理者某个具体数值例子该怎么做，还能解释当库存、成本、提前期或风险变化时，行动应该怎样变化。</span></p>
        <p><span class="ui-copy-en">When no clean structure survives, the field moves toward dynamic programming, decomposition, simulation, heuristics, approximate dynamic programming, or learning-based policies. The computational method is therefore closely tied to what structure the model retains.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">当简单结构不再成立时，研究才会进一步转向动态规划、分解、仿真、启发式方法、近似动态规划或学习型策略。因此，计算方法并不是与理论结构分离的另一件事，它往往取决于模型还剩下多少可以利用的结构。</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="field-guide-process" style="--guide-steps:5">
        <div class="field-guide-step"><b>01</b><span><span class="ui-copy-en">Observe inventory & pipeline</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">观察库存与在途量</span></span></div>
        <div class="field-guide-step is-focus"><b>02</b><span><span class="ui-copy-en">Choose replenishment</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">决定补货</span></span></div>
        <div class="field-guide-step"><b>03</b><span><span class="ui-copy-en">Demand arrives</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">需求发生</span></span></div>
        <div class="field-guide-step"><b>04</b><span><span class="ui-copy-en">Costs & service realized</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">成本与服务结果实现</span></span></div>
        <div class="field-guide-step"><b>05</b><span><span class="ui-copy-en">State updates</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">系统进入下一状态</span></span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="field-guide-section">
      <div class="field-guide-section-head">
        <span class="field-guide-index">05</span>
        <div>
          <h2><span class="ui-copy-en">Where the field is used — and where research keeps moving</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">库存理论用在哪里，又还在研究什么？</span></h2>
          <p><span class="ui-copy-en">The same inventory logic appears in very different industries, but modern systems keep adding new information, new constraints, and new interactions.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">同一套库存逻辑会出现在很多行业，而现代系统不断加入新的信息、新的约束与新的相互作用。</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="field-guide-atlas">
        <article class="field-guide-card"><small>retail</small><h3><span class="ui-copy-en">Omnichannel & fulfillment</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">零售与全渠道履约</span></h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Where should stock sit when the same item serves stores, online orders, pickup, and returns?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">当同一件商品同时服务门店、线上订单、自提与退货时，库存应该放在哪里？</span></p></article>
        <article class="field-guide-card"><small>manufacturing</small><h3><span class="ui-copy-en">Components & production</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">制造与零部件</span></h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Inventory interacts with setup decisions, capacity, bills of materials, production sequencing, and supplier reliability.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">库存会与启动成本、产能、物料清单、生产顺序和供应商可靠性共同决定生产系统表现。</span></p></article>
        <article class="field-guide-card"><small>healthcare</small><h3><span class="ui-copy-en">Critical supplies</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">医疗关键物资</span></h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Shortages can be far more costly than holding stock, while perishability and emergency demand make overstocking costly too.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">缺货的代价可能极高，但保质期与突发需求又让过量备货同样昂贵。</span></p></article>
        <article class="field-guide-card"><small>service</small><h3><span class="ui-copy-en">Spare parts & reliability</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">备件与可靠性</span></h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Demand is often sparse and failure-driven. Installed-base information, repair loops, and service targets become central.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">需求往往低频且由失效驱动，在役设备信息、维修循环与服务水平成为核心。</span></p></article>
        <article class="field-guide-card"><small>data-driven</small><h3><span class="ui-copy-en">Learning while controlling</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">边学习边决策</span></h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">The system may need to learn demand or failure parameters from observations while simultaneously making replenishment decisions.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">系统可能一边从观测中学习需求或失效参数，一边仍然必须持续做补货决策。</span></p></article>
        <article class="field-guide-card"><small>resilience</small><h3><span class="ui-copy-en">Disruption & robustness</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">中断与韧性</span></h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Supply shocks, uncertain lead times, geopolitical disruptions, and rare events raise questions about how much protection a system should carry.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">供应冲击、随机提前期、地缘中断与极端事件都会重新提出一个问题：系统究竟应该为韧性准备多少缓冲？</span></p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="field-guide-section">
      <div class="field-guide-section-head">
        <span class="field-guide-index">06</span>
        <div>
          <h2><span class="ui-copy-en">Where my current work sits</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">我的当前研究落在这张地图的哪里？</span></h2>
          <p><span class="ui-copy-en">Warranty inventory is one corner of the much broader inventory field: a service-parts problem in which future demand is generated by failures of products already in the installed base.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">保修库存只是整个库存理论中的一个角落：它属于售后备件与服务库存问题，而且未来需求由已经售出的在役产品失效所产生。</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="field-guide-callout">
        <small><span class="ui-copy-en">My research lens</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">我的研究切口</span></small>
        <strong><span class="ui-copy-en">Warranty adds memory to service demand.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">保修让售后需求带上了“历史记忆”。</span></strong>
        <p><span class="ui-copy-en">Past sales, product ages, and failure behavior can affect future replacement demand. That makes state representation, structural policy analysis, and approximation especially important. The broader inventory map above is the context; warranty is the particular mechanism I am currently trying to understand.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">过去卖出了多少产品、这些产品处在什么年龄、怎样失效，都可能影响未来替换需求。因此状态表示、策略结构与近似方法会变得格外重要。上面的整张库存理论地图是背景，而保修机制只是我目前正在深入研究的一个具体切口。</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="field-guide-links">
        <a href="https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/esd-260j-logistics-systems-fall-2006/pages/lecture-notes/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><small>MIT OpenCourseWare</small><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">Inventory management lecture sequence</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">库存管理课程资料</span></strong><span><span class="ui-copy-en">EOQ, stochastic demand, safety stock, special products, and inventory in practice.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">覆盖 EOQ、随机需求、安全库存、特殊产品与库存实践。</span></span></a>
        <a href="https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/esd-273j-logistics-and-supply-chain-management-fall-2009/pages/readings/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><small>MIT · Simchi-Levi</small><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">Logistics & supply-chain inventory models</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">物流与供应链库存模型</span></strong><span><span class="ui-copy-en">A broader course map from deterministic inventory to stochastic and multi-period models.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">从确定性库存到随机、多周期模型的一张更完整课程地图。</span></span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="field-guide-back">
      <a href={withBase('/research')}>← <span class="ui-copy-en">Back to Research</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">返回研究主页</span></a>
      <a href={withBase('/research/stochastic-optimization')}><span class="ui-copy-en">Next: Stochastic Optimization →</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">下一篇：随机优化 →</span></a>
    </div>
  </main>
  <SiteExtras />
</BaseLayout>
